9539	You can make it possible for new users to register themselves for accounts, with or without email verification or administrative approval. Or, you can make it so only administrators with <em>Administer users</em> permission can register new users.		11.1.5
9540	You can configure what happens to content that a user created, if their account is <em>canceled</em> (deleted).		11.1.5
9541	What are variables in email message text?		11.1.5
9542	<em>Variables</em> are short text strings, enclosed in square brackets [], that you can insert into configured email message text. When an individual message is generated, data from your site is substituted for the variables. Some commonly-used variables are:		11.1.5
9543	[site:name]: The name of your website.		11.1.5
9544	[site:url]: The URL of your website.		11.1.5
9545	[site:login-url]: The URL where users can log in to your site.		11.1.5
9546	[user:display-name]: The user's displayed name.		11.1.5
9547	[user:mail]: The user's email alias.		11.1.5
9548	[user:one-time-login-url]: An expiring URL that a user can use to log in once, if they need to reset their password.		11.1.5
9549	In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>People</em> &gt; <em>@account_settings_link</em>.		11.1.5
